# The house style of dm/ as clang-format can state it: 4-space indents, attached braces, no column limit (lines run as long as their thought), short blocks, ifs, loops
# and functions kept on one line, case labels at the switch's own indent, comments, includes and preprocessor indents left as written. CI (.github/workflows/lint-c.yml,
# dm/tools/lint_c.py format) applies it to the lines a pull request changes only, and reports only spacing inside a line: clang-format puts every statement on a line of its
# own, which the dense style here does not, so its line breaks are not reported. Existing code is not reformatted.
BasedOnStyle: LLVM
IndentWidth: 4
ObjCBlockIndentWidth: 4
ColumnLimit: 0
AllowShortFunctionsOnASingleLine: All
AllowShortBlocksOnASingleLine: Always
AllowShortIfStatementsOnASingleLine: AllIfsAndElse
AllowShortLoopsOnASingleLine: true
AllowShortCaseLabelsOnASingleLine: true
AllowShortEnumsOnASingleLine: true
IndentCaseLabels: false
IndentPPDirectives: Leave
SortIncludes: Never
ReflowComments: false
AlignTrailingComments:
  Kind: Leave
SpacesBeforeTrailingComments: 1
AlignEscapedNewlines: DontAlign
BreakStringLiterals: false
MaxEmptyLinesToKeep: 2
SpacesInContainerLiterals: false
